25
00:06:02,629 --> 00:06:05,149
<v TUTOR> Yes that would add a bit of variety.

26
00:06:05,433 --> 00:06:17,737
<v MARTIN> Then the section on further research carried out on the island – analysing the mud in the lake. I wonder if we’ve actually got too much information here, should we cut some?

27
00:06:17,914 --> 00:06:22,132
<v ROSIE> I don’t think so, but it’s all a bit muddled at present.

28
00:06:22,282 --> 00:06:26,520
<v MARTIN> Yes, maybe it would be better if it followed a chronological pattern.

29
00:06:26,634 --> 00:06:36,314
<v ROSIE> I think so. The findings and possible explanations section is just about ready, but we need to practice it so we’re sure it won’t overrun.

30
00:06:36,489 --> 00:06:40,464
<v MARTIN> I think it should be OK, but yes, let’s make sure.

31
